      {
        "y": 356.5,
        "x0": 74.7,
        "x1": 304.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "B Words and expressions about clothes"
      },
      {
        "y": 373.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 512.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Clothes can be described as revealing1, skimpy2, baggy3, clingy4, or chic5. Sometimes an invitation"
      },
      {
        "y": 385.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 501.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "to a more formal party will ask people to dress in smart-casual6 clothes. To be dolled (up) / dressed"
      },
      {
        "y": 398.2,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 511,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "up / done up to the nines means to be dressed in a very fashionable or very formal way. Some people"
      },
      {
        "y": 410.2,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 498.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "choose to buy designer (label) clothes but most people prefer to buy clothes more cheaply on the"
      },
      {
        "y": 421.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 502.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "High Street7. People who can afford to sometimes have clothes made-to-measure8, but more often"
      },
      {
        "y": 433.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 272.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "people buy their clothes off the peg/rack9."
